# N-Triples lines that must be rejected. One per line; each is parsed on its own.
# Derived from the grammar in https://www.w3.org/TR/n-triples/#n-triples-grammar
# A malformed line must fail loudly — silently skipping one would build a graph from part of a
# document, which is the same failure mode the journal forbids.

<https://example.org/s> <https://example.org/p> <https://example.org/o>
<https://example.org/s> <https://example.org/p> .
<https://example.org/s> <https://example.org/p> <https://example.org/o> <https://example.org/g> .
https://example.org/s <https://example.org/p> <https://example.org/o> .
<https://example.org/s <https://example.org/p> <https://example.org/o> .
<https://example.org/s> "literal predicates are not allowed" <https://example.org/o> .
<https://example.org/s> <https://example.org/p> "unterminated .
<https://example.org/s> <https://example.org/p> "bad escape \q" .
<https://example.org/s> <https://example.org/p> "truncated \u12" .
<https://example.org/s> <https://example.org/p> "not hex \uZZZZ" .
<https://example.org/s> <https://example.org/p> "dangling escape \" .
<https://example.org/s> <https://example.org/p> "tagged"@ .
<https://example.org/s> <https://example.org/p> "tagged"@en_US .
<https://example.org/s> <https://example.org/p> "tagged"@toolongalanguage .
